// boxcxx — <__bits/version_span>
//
// The one feature-test macro [version.syn] gives <span>: P0122R7's span,
// at its C++20 value with P2116R0's deduction guides folded in. Split into a
// leaf for the same [support.limits.general] per-header reason as every other
// version_* file -- see <__bits/version_any> for the full explanation.
//
// It was withheld on three things this document also got partly wrong. The
// claim that span had no crbegin/crend was stale -- both were there. What
// was genuinely missing: the iterator constructors took POINTERS rather than
// an iterator and a sentinel, they were not explicit(extent !=
// dynamic_extent), and the range deduction guide did not exist, so
// `std::span(v)` over a vector could not deduce at all. Ф31e-g closed those.
//
// Every block below is gated on BOXCXX_OWNS_<stem>, and this file has NO
// include guard: it is meant to be included once per owning header, each time
// defining only what that header declared it owns. [support.limits.general]
// says a macro is defined by <version> AND by the header that provides the
// feature; it does not say every header that happens to include this leaf.
// A header that answers for a feature it does not provide is answering a
// question it was not asked, so it no longer does. <version> defines
// BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL and takes the lot. Checked by tools/cxx_ftm_audit.sh.

#if (defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_ALL) || defined(BOXCXX_OWNS_span)) && \
    !defined(__cpp_lib_span)
// P2821R5's span::at has been in the tree since Ф31e-g-1 -- the member was
// there and the macro was not, which is the one direction of mismatch this
// file exists to prevent. Verified against the member, then raised (Ф32-e).
#  define __cpp_lib_span 202311L
#endif
#undef BOXCXX_OWNS_span
